.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt PISCSI-OLED 1
.Os PiSCSI
.Sh NAME
.Nm piscsi-oled
.Nd display PiSCSI status on an SSD1306 I2C OLED panel
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl diagnostic
.Op Fl height Ar 32|64
.Op Fl host Ar HOST
.Op Fl i2c-address Ar ADDRESS
.Op Fl i2c-device Ar DEVICE
.Op Fl password Ar TOKEN
.Op Fl port Ar PORT
.Op Fl refresh_interval Ar MILLISECONDS
.Op Fl rotation Ar 0|180
.Op Fl screensaver Ar off|ip|blank
.Op Fl screensaver-idle-timeout Ar DURATION
.Op Fl screensaver-move-interval Ar DURATION
.Op Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
polls a PiSCSI daemon and presents its current status on a 128-by-32 or
128-by-64 SSD1306 OLED display connected through I2C.
It shows startup and shutdown splash screens, rotates long status lines, and
can activate an optional screensaver after status has been unchanged for a
period of time.
.Pp
The default display is a 128-by-32 panel at address 0x3c on
.Pa /dev/i2c-1 ,
rotated 180 degrees.
The default daemon is
.Dq localhost
on port 6868.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl diagnostic
Show the startup and shutdown splashes, clear the display, and exit without
contacting the PiSCSI daemon.
.It Fl height Ar 32|64
Display height in pixels.
The default is 32.
.It Fl host Ar HOST
PiSCSI daemon hostname.
The default is
.Dq localhost .
.It Fl horizontal_scroll_step Ar PIXELS
Pixels by which long lines move after each refresh.
Specify 0 to pause horizontal scrolling.
The default is 6.
.It Fl i2c-address Ar ADDRESS
SSD1306 I2C address, expressed as an integer accepted by Go, such as
.Dq 0x3c .
.It Fl i2c-device Ar DEVICE
Linux I2C device.
The default is
.Pa /dev/i2c-1 .
.It Fl password Ar TOKEN
PiSCSI daemon authentication token.
.It Fl port Ar PORT
PiSCSI daemon port.
The default is 6868.
.It Fl refresh_interval Ar MILLISECONDS
Screen refresh interval in milliseconds.
0 uses the minimum interval of one millisecond.
The default is 1000.
.It Fl rotation Ar 0|180
Screen rotation in degrees.
The default is 180.
.It Fl screensaver Ar off|ip|blank
Screensaver mode.
.Dq ip
keeps the network-status line visible and moves it periodically;
.Dq blank
clears the display;
.Dq off
disables the screensaver.
The default is
.Dq off .
.It Fl screensaver-idle-timeout Ar DURATION
Time for which the status must remain unchanged before the screensaver starts.
The default is 5m.
.It Fl screensaver-move-interval Ar DURATION
Interval between moves of the IP screensaver line.
The default is 30s.
.It Fl v
Print PiSCSI version and copyright information, then exit.
.El
.Pp
Duration options accept Go duration strings, for example 30s, 5m, and 1h.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Use a 128-by-64 display rotated 180 degrees:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
piscsi-oled -height=64 -rotation=180
.Ed
.Pp
Enable the IP screensaver after five minutes of inactivity:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
piscsi-oled -screensaver=ip -screensaver-idle-timeout=5m
.Ed
.Sh HARDWARE
Enable I2C before using the program and ensure that the service account can
access the selected I2C device.
On Raspberry Pi OS, the display is usually available at
.Pa /dev/i2c-1 .
Use
.Xr i2cdetect 8
to identify its address.
.Sh SIGNALS
.Nm
handles
.Dv SIGINT
and
.Dv SIGTERM .
It displays the shutdown splash, clears the OLED panel, and exits.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr piscsi 1 ,
.Xr i2cdetect 8
.Pp
Full documentation is available at: <https://www.piscsi.com>
